WEBVTT

00:16.970 --> 00:20.100
-Now, who shall we choose?
-How exciting.

00:20.180 --> 00:24.520
<i>At that moment, my brain couldn't comprehend what had happened.</i>

00:24.600 --> 00:26.980
I think we should choose him.

00:27.060 --> 00:30.820
What a coincidence, I want him too.

00:30.900 --> 00:34.570
<i>I couldn't comprehend the meaning of losing here.</i>

00:34.660 --> 00:35.610
Come.

00:35.700 --> 00:37.070
Bachira Meguru.

00:40.200 --> 00:41.870
Hurry up so we can advance.

00:41.950 --> 00:43.580
Don't zone out, bowl cut.

00:45.370 --> 00:50.630
Until the very end, I wanted to be with Isagi.

00:51.760 --> 00:54.010
I have to go, it's the rule.

00:55.930 --> 00:59.010
But I won't wait for you, Isagi.

00:59.810 --> 01:02.310
If you want me, come and get me.

01:05.270 --> 01:06.440
<i>From now on,</i>

01:07.020 --> 01:08.310
<i>I'll chase after.</i>

01:09.730 --> 01:13.990
<i>To get back the precious thing I lost.</i>

02:53.880 --> 02:55.670
2ND STAGE 2-ON-2 RIVALRY BATTLE
MATCHING ROOM

02:55.750 --> 02:59.430
So when you lose at 3-on-3, you end up here.

03:00.550 --> 03:02.640
Seems like we're the first ones here.

03:03.720 --> 03:04.560
Yeah.

03:05.810 --> 03:06.890
What should we do?

03:07.470 --> 03:09.640
Looks like there's a place to rest.

03:09.730 --> 03:10.656
Should we go check it out?

03:11.190 --> 03:13.110
Is this really the time to rest?

03:13.770 --> 03:15.820
If we lose again, we're done.

03:16.400 --> 03:20.150
We'll win next time. Our opponents were just too strong this time.

03:21.660 --> 03:23.370
That's not the point.

03:24.070 --> 03:25.780
I'm different from you.

03:26.580 --> 03:27.490
I,

03:28.410 --> 03:31.460
<i>I couldn't do anything against them.</i>

03:33.250 --> 03:36.630
What are you talking about? You scored a goal too.

03:36.710 --> 03:39.550
That was the result of our three-man team play.

03:40.113 --> 03:41.923
Isn't that what soccer is all about?

03:42.007 --> 03:42.920
No!

03:43.260 --> 03:45.180
I'm talking about how I couldn't fight

03:45.260 --> 03:47.470
when our team play was shut down!

03:47.560 --> 03:52.190
<i>I couldn't create a chemical reaction like you and Bachira did.</i>

03:52.770 --> 03:53.900
That's all there is to it.

03:54.520 --> 03:58.650
If we lose again, the one who'll be chosen is you, Nagi.

03:59.940 --> 04:01.400
I won't be chosen.

04:02.280 --> 04:04.642
If I were them, I wouldn't choose myself either.

04:06.531 --> 04:07.884
Are you kidding me, Isagi?

04:08.620 --> 04:11.080
If you're in this state, what about me?

04:12.410 --> 04:16.880
I joined you thinking I'd become stronger if I played with you.

04:17.630 --> 04:20.130
But you being this weak just gets in my way.

04:21.220 --> 04:22.880
Get a hold of yourself, you leech.

04:22.970 --> 04:26.350
What, so you're blaming me?

04:26.430 --> 04:27.640
Put in more effort.

04:28.430 --> 04:30.350
Reo wouldn't have been this weak.

04:31.680 --> 04:34.730
What's that supposed to mean? Go team up with Reo then!

04:34.810 --> 04:37.363
Don't just compare us on a whim and force your ideals on me!

04:37.860 --> 04:42.190
What else can I do? I've never played soccer with anyone else before him.

04:43.030 --> 04:46.030
So you're useless without Reo?

04:46.740 --> 04:51.000
You're saying that, even though you're useless without Bachira?

04:53.210 --> 04:54.420
Stop.

04:55.250 --> 04:56.670
You're right.

04:56.750 --> 04:58.750
That's what's pissing me off.

04:58.840 --> 04:59.800
Damn it!

05:01.630 --> 05:04.170
If you want me, come and get me.

05:05.050 --> 05:08.890
I'll follow the monster inside me.

05:09.760 --> 05:11.220
<i>What's wrong with him?</i>

05:12.270 --> 05:18.060
I'll show that I can fight even without Bachira.

05:19.900 --> 05:23.280
Is that what this selection is about?

05:23.360 --> 05:24.360
What?

05:24.450 --> 05:27.530
I still don't understand soccer very well, but

05:28.280 --> 05:31.370
<i>until now, as long as there was someone who made one from zero,</i>

05:31.450 --> 05:35.370
<i>it was enough for the others to play in a way that elevated that one to a hundred.</i>

05:36.210 --> 05:40.420
<i>But in the second selection, there are fewer players and the field is smaller.</i>

05:40.500 --> 05:41.960
<i>Individual play</i>

05:42.050 --> 05:44.300
<i>has a much greater impact.</i>

05:44.880 --> 05:47.010
What's being tested is our individual skills.

05:47.760 --> 05:48.640
I see.

05:49.260 --> 05:51.010
What we were trying to do,

05:51.100 --> 05:54.560
we couldn't get anywhere with assists or set plays.

05:55.140 --> 05:55.980
Yeah.

05:56.480 --> 05:58.900
It might work against weaker opponents, but

05:59.560 --> 06:03.280
from now on, individual battles will be at the forefront.

06:04.190 --> 06:07.360
<i>no matter who your teammates or opponents are,</i>

06:07.950 --> 06:09.700
<i>you have to win your one-on-ones.</i>

06:09.780 --> 06:11.950
<i>That's the key to surviving the second selection.</i>

06:12.950 --> 06:15.080
There's one more thing, Isagi.

06:15.660 --> 06:18.710
How do I get rid of this feeling of anger?

06:21.090 --> 06:23.340
I'm sorry, but Nagi,

06:24.170 --> 06:25.010
by winning.

06:25.590 --> 06:27.510
Otherwise, this pain won't go away.

06:31.260 --> 06:32.640
Barou.

06:32.720 --> 06:34.310
What do you know.

06:34.390 --> 06:37.940
So if your team sucks, you get thrown into a place like this.

06:38.600 --> 06:41.770
Isn't there anyone strong here?

06:41.860 --> 06:43.820
<i>The key to passing the second selection</i>

06:43.900 --> 06:45.820
<i>is individual strength.</i>

06:45.900 --> 06:48.200
<i>If I can't become strong enough to beat this guy</i>

06:48.280 --> 06:50.030
<i>-I can't survive.</i>
-Get out of my way.

06:50.110 --> 06:53.580
<i>But how can I win against Barou?</i>

06:54.740 --> 06:59.080
It's pretty surprising you're here. Weren't you the strongest?

06:59.160 --> 07:00.460
Want to play with us?

07:01.380 --> 07:03.420
I think I can beat you right now.

07:05.340 --> 07:07.670
Who's beating who?

07:07.760 --> 07:09.720
Me and Isagi, you.

07:10.300 --> 07:13.510
You, who's nothing more than ball control,

07:13.600 --> 07:17.430
shall I personally crush you as the king?

07:18.100 --> 07:20.730
You still call yourself a king even after losing.

07:21.600 --> 07:24.020
I'll defeat you and make you my servant.

07:24.110 --> 07:26.320
Wait, Nagi. Don't provoke him.

07:26.400 --> 07:28.490
<i>I still don't believe I can beat Barou.</i>

07:28.570 --> 07:30.030
'Before the next match,

07:30.110 --> 07:36.080
you must wait 24 hours.' It says.

07:36.160 --> 07:37.370
I'm talking to both of you.

07:38.040 --> 07:39.330
Naruhaya!

07:39.410 --> 07:40.750
Who was that?

07:40.830 --> 07:42.790
My former teammate.

07:43.420 --> 07:45.630
More importantly, you teamed up with Barou?

07:46.670 --> 07:51.380
The other guy was Nishioka, the Messi of Aomori,

07:51.470 --> 07:55.470
<i>but as soon as the match started, Barou scored 4 goals straight away.</i>

07:55.550 --> 07:58.310
But the other team scored 5, so we lost.

07:59.020 --> 08:00.770
Since Barou played too selfishly,

08:00.850 --> 08:02.640
they didn't choose him thinking he'd disrupt the balance.

08:02.730 --> 08:04.440
So the two of us were left.

08:04.520 --> 08:08.030
We lost because you're talentless.

08:08.110 --> 08:10.240
Stop making stupid moves.

08:10.320 --> 08:13.030
Come on, let's just calm down for now.

08:13.110 --> 08:16.160
There's no need to rush and clash with them.

08:16.240 --> 08:18.277
After all, it's over if we lose again.

08:19.240 --> 08:21.000
Right, Isagi?

08:21.080 --> 08:23.370
What? Yeah.

08:26.170 --> 08:28.130
I'm not running or hiding.

08:28.960 --> 08:30.960
If you want to get crushed, come at me anytime.

08:32.260 --> 08:33.680
Losers.

08:33.760 --> 08:35.680
See you later, Isagi!

08:35.760 --> 08:36.600
Okay.

08:40.100 --> 08:41.390
Look, Isagi.

08:42.060 --> 08:43.390
A prison, sideways.

08:43.480 --> 08:45.900
After all, this place is a 'Blue Prison'.

08:46.480 --> 08:49.190
There's a regular bath and cafeteria, but

08:49.270 --> 08:52.150
compared to before, the quality seems to have dropped.

08:52.240 --> 08:54.490
The biggest difference is

08:54.570 --> 08:58.450
that we can use the Blue Lock Men in the training room.

08:58.530 --> 08:59.580
Hey, Isagi.

09:00.160 --> 09:02.450
Why didn't you say let's clash with Barou?

09:03.540 --> 09:05.920
I thought it would be good to add him to our team.

09:06.750 --> 09:10.340
That's true, but in our current state...

09:10.420 --> 09:12.970
What exactly are we lacking?

09:14.123 --> 09:16.530
What I realized in our match against Rin's team,

09:17.140 --> 09:21.140
our weapons can only be utilized as long as we receive passes.

09:21.720 --> 09:23.390
Now I understand.

09:23.480 --> 09:27.440
<i>Mine is ball control and yours is the direct shot.</i>

09:28.150 --> 09:29.480
Yes.

09:29.570 --> 09:33.860
Unless there is someone who understands our weapons like Bachira and Reo,

09:33.940 --> 09:38.700
meaning someone with great passes, we can't stand out.

09:41.080 --> 09:45.910
So how do we use our weapons without passes?

09:46.750 --> 09:49.380
Dribbling, agility,

09:49.460 --> 09:52.710
long limbs, monstrous strength...

09:53.460 --> 09:56.970
We have no chance of winning against those in a one-on-one.

09:57.050 --> 09:59.640
That's precisely what we're lacking.

09:59.720 --> 10:02.640
How do we win one-on-ones without passes?

10:03.970 --> 10:06.440
That's so much harder.

10:06.520 --> 10:09.100
Sorry, it seemed like too much of a hassle.

10:09.900 --> 10:11.860
We'll think about it tomorrow.

10:12.440 --> 10:13.570
Yeah, you're right.

10:19.740 --> 10:20.910
He looks like a mummy.

10:24.120 --> 10:25.700
How can we win?

10:25.790 --> 10:28.120
What does one-on-one strength even mean?

10:30.540 --> 10:32.420
2ND STAGE
CAFETERIA

10:34.420 --> 10:37.670
Those who lost and dropped stages are packed in here.

10:37.760 --> 10:41.430
But more importantly, Isagi, this is a disaster. This cafeteria,

10:41.510 --> 10:44.010
they only serve natto and pickled radish.

10:45.470 --> 10:47.730
Fool, I got used to it a long time ago.

10:48.480 --> 10:50.850
So what are we going to do, Isagi?

10:51.520 --> 10:53.070
Which team will we clash with?

10:53.150 --> 10:54.230
Well,

10:54.320 --> 10:58.320
if we choose a team weaker than us, it'd be easy, but

10:58.900 --> 11:02.660
adding such a person to our team won't be useful later on

11:02.740 --> 11:04.740
and we'll end up back at this point.

11:04.830 --> 11:08.870
<i>Also, at that moment, I'd probably lose Nagi.</i>

11:09.620 --> 11:11.330
It's better to beat the strong ones

11:11.420 --> 11:13.460
and add them to our team, but

11:13.540 --> 11:17.420
since our chances of losing increase, we can't just pair with anyone randomly.

11:18.550 --> 11:22.800
Seems like everyone is thinking the same thing and assessing the situation.

11:22.890 --> 11:23.930
Yeah.

11:25.140 --> 11:29.560
<i>This is the essence of the rivalry battle. Rather than just winning,</i>

11:29.640 --> 11:33.980
<i>we can't move forward without considering how useful the person we team up with will be.</i>

11:38.490 --> 11:41.490
<i>My direct shots are improving.</i>

11:42.160 --> 11:46.410
<i>But I couldn't do anything in a real match.</i>

11:46.490 --> 11:52.370
<i>They have the talent to dominate one-on-ones and create chances.</i>

11:52.460 --> 11:56.500
<i>The ones I have to surpass are these monsters.</i>

11:57.960 --> 12:01.380
<i>The power to dominate in one-on-ones and create chances.</i>

12:01.470 --> 12:06.720
<i>To find the clue to do that, I might have to clash with him again.</i>

12:07.890 --> 12:09.560
Ah, found you.

12:09.640 --> 12:11.690
You're working hard, Isagi.

12:11.770 --> 12:12.980
Naruhaya.

12:13.060 --> 12:15.270
Have you decided on your next opponent?

12:15.360 --> 12:17.690
No, not yet.

12:17.770 --> 12:19.900
Is that so?

12:19.990 --> 12:23.450
If we lose once more, we're finished. It's really nerve-wracking.

12:23.530 --> 12:27.780
True, but I still don't want to add a weak player to the team.

12:27.870 --> 12:31.370
Yeah. So I've been thinking,

12:31.460 --> 12:34.750
we need to take a risk.

12:36.000 --> 12:37.340
In what sense?

12:37.920 --> 12:43.550
After all, you and I are the ones who won't be chosen if we lose.

12:45.090 --> 12:47.680
We're the same, right?

12:48.430 --> 12:50.560
Scary, isn't it?

12:50.640 --> 12:53.980
My teammate is Barou, and yours is Nagi, man.

12:54.640 --> 12:57.360
In this situation, there's no way we'd be chosen.

12:58.110 --> 13:00.820
Maybe for you, but you're still...

13:00.900 --> 13:04.110
No need for politeness.

13:04.200 --> 13:07.410
After all, the one I want,

13:08.120 --> 13:08.997
is Nagi.

13:09.830 --> 13:12.410
It's not you, Isagi.

13:14.410 --> 13:16.290
You should have realized too.

13:16.920 --> 13:22.300
If you don't add truly strong ones to your team, you can't move forward.

13:23.090 --> 13:27.720
Also, if you want to realize your dream of becoming the world's best striker,

13:27.800 --> 13:29.760
you can't hold back here.

13:29.850 --> 13:31.180
If you run, it's over.

13:32.100 --> 13:34.270
Let's crush each other, Isagi.

13:35.140 --> 13:37.020
Our dreams are at stake.

13:38.100 --> 13:39.860
Don't be a coward.

13:39.940 --> 13:41.780
This is Blue Lock.

13:43.110 --> 13:44.190
<i>This guy...</i>

13:45.400 --> 13:49.990
It suits me. Actually, I was hoping to play against you too.

13:50.080 --> 13:51.209
Then it's decided.

13:51.910 --> 13:54.370
YOICHI ISAGI & SEISHIRO NAGI VS ASAHI NARUHAYA & SHOUEI BAROU

13:54.450 --> 13:56.960
MATCHING APPROVED

14:04.510 --> 14:05.670
Come on, Isagi.

14:05.760 --> 14:07.760
-This is your 50th attempt.
-Okay!

14:09.090 --> 14:10.140
Too obvious.

14:11.640 --> 14:15.180
Barou's weapon is his super accurate mid-range shot.

14:15.270 --> 14:18.850
<i>A shot from the left side of the goal, with a maximum range of 27 meters.</i>

14:19.650 --> 14:21.820
<i>Also, thanks to his extraordinary physique,</i>

14:21.900 --> 14:23.860
<i>he crushes his way into that range.</i>

14:23.940 --> 14:25.490
Right?

14:25.570 --> 14:26.700
Correct.

14:26.780 --> 14:30.490
This is bad, Isagi. I can't practice this against you.

14:31.950 --> 14:35.370
I don't care about playing them, but do you have a plan?

14:35.450 --> 14:38.080
Honestly, I won't know until we face them.

14:38.160 --> 14:39.670
Yeah, you're right.

14:40.098 --> 14:43.098
Unlike a normal match, the teams here are much smaller.

14:43.563 --> 14:46.613
That's why one-on-one encounters become so much more important.

14:46.970 --> 14:47.821
Right.

14:48.380 --> 14:52.930
The only way to figure out how to beat Barou is to play against him.

14:53.010 --> 14:54.890
It's a total gamble.

14:55.810 --> 14:57.390
For us to survive,

14:57.980 --> 15:01.310
<i>we'll need to find the individual strength to beat Barou</i>

15:01.400 --> 15:04.150
<i>during the match.</i>

15:04.230 --> 15:06.940
Alright, I'll start the match marking Barou.

15:07.610 --> 15:09.780
Isagi, you take the small fry.

15:09.860 --> 15:10.910
Got it.

15:11.870 --> 15:14.240
Let's crush each other, Isagi.

15:14.990 --> 15:16.790
Our dreams are at stake.

15:17.540 --> 15:22.210
<i>Crushing these guys will allow me to improve myself and advance to the next stage.</i>

15:22.290 --> 15:24.420
<i>If I lose here,</i>

15:24.500 --> 15:27.130
<i>it means this is the limit of my ability.</i>

15:27.210 --> 15:29.130
That's enough, small fry.

15:29.220 --> 15:30.470
I'm going to sleep.

15:31.300 --> 15:33.890
Don't get in my way during tomorrow's match.

15:34.470 --> 15:36.810
Go play somewhere else, loser.

15:37.470 --> 15:39.640
Understood, king.

15:44.020 --> 15:45.190
Damn it.

15:47.360 --> 15:51.110
I don't want it to end yet.

15:51.200 --> 15:52.360
CARAMEL

15:58.080 --> 15:59.750
TIME REMAINING UNTIL THE MATCH

15:59.830 --> 16:03.210
2ND STAGE
2-ON-2 RIVALRY BATTLE

16:03.290 --> 16:05.290
I've been looking forward to this, king.

16:05.380 --> 16:07.210
Did you practice kneeling?

16:07.300 --> 16:09.300
You're dead.

16:09.380 --> 16:11.550
You're going to be my slave.

16:11.630 --> 16:12.550
Naruhaya.

16:14.840 --> 16:18.100
I'm really going to crush you, so don't hold back.

16:20.640 --> 16:22.270
You didn't have to say that.

16:27.900 --> 16:30.030
<i>He has a crazy stance.</i>

16:30.110 --> 16:31.610
Bring it on, king.

16:31.700 --> 16:33.150
Let's go one-on-one.

16:33.240 --> 16:35.518
<i>If I can't beat him, I won't get anywhere.</i>

16:35.608 --> 16:37.490
You call that dribbling?

16:37.580 --> 16:39.450
Your timing and use of space are trash.

16:40.250 --> 16:42.500
Do you realize who you're facing?

16:43.670 --> 16:46.330
Show some respect.

16:46.420 --> 16:48.000
Damn. Isagi!

16:48.090 --> 16:50.090
<i>Seriously? I have to stop him.</i>

16:50.710 --> 16:52.220
<i>Naruhaya made his move too.</i>

16:52.300 --> 16:54.130
<i>What should I do now? No.</i>

16:54.220 --> 16:57.800
<i>I should stay put. Barou's range is 27 meters.</i>

16:58.970 --> 17:02.390
<i>What? This is 28... No, the distance should be at least 29 meters, right?</i>

17:08.570 --> 17:12.070
<i>So Barou is improving himself in Blue Lock too.</i>

17:12.150 --> 17:16.200
This is not good, Isagi. His range is gradually increasing.

17:16.280 --> 17:17.410
Yeah.

17:17.490 --> 17:21.580
<i>Still, I have to figure something out during the match. I will figure it out.</i>

17:23.251 --> 17:25.580
<i>I'll find a way to win one-on-ones.</i>

17:25.670 --> 17:29.090
<i>Leaving Barou aside, if I can get past this guy one-on-one,</i>

17:29.170 --> 17:30.672
<i>we'll have a fifty-fifty chance.</i>

17:32.300 --> 17:34.380
<i>Damn it, he's so persistent.</i>

17:34.470 --> 17:37.180
<i>Is my dribbling insufficient even against Naruhaya?</i>

17:37.260 --> 17:40.350
<i>So should I send it exactly where Nagi wants?</i>

17:40.430 --> 17:44.060
<i>No, I'm not skilled enough to deliver such a pass.</i>

17:44.140 --> 17:46.390
<i>Naruhaya is blocking the passing lanes</i>

17:46.480 --> 17:49.860
<i>and Barou will intercept any inaccurate pass.</i>

17:49.940 --> 17:51.860
<i>Crap! What should I do?</i>

17:53.150 --> 17:55.900
Pass, Isagi. It doesn't matter how, just pass to me...

17:56.490 --> 17:57.740
Pass to the opening you see!

17:59.200 --> 18:01.490
Where are you passing, loser?

18:01.580 --> 18:04.580
You can't get past me with such a weak pass.

18:04.660 --> 18:06.290
I know, king.

18:06.370 --> 18:08.750
Forget him, I've finally found it.

18:09.790 --> 18:11.420
How to defeat you.

18:12.340 --> 18:16.970
<i>When I move forward and stop, I can't avoid Barou's individual pressure.</i>

18:17.050 --> 18:19.510
<i>So the trick is to make them follow me.</i>

18:20.260 --> 18:23.180
<i>Because that's what happened back then too.</i>

18:23.260 --> 18:27.810
<i>The things I did instinctively are starting to make sense.</i>

18:29.020 --> 18:32.320
<i>They're becoming a reproducible formula.</i>

18:33.730 --> 18:35.650
<i>I don't need special passes.</i>

18:36.320 --> 18:40.450
<i>I can bring the ball to life with my first touch.</i>

18:40.530 --> 18:42.660
<i>Did you see my rhythm?</i>

18:42.740 --> 18:44.370
<i>Take it if you can, king.</i>

18:45.700 --> 18:47.620
<i>I am the god of this field.</i>

18:48.920 --> 18:52.290
<i>Nagi, at what speed are you evolving?</i>

18:58.130 --> 18:59.510
We can win this, Isagi.

19:00.340 --> 19:02.010
The rest is up to you.

19:02.100 --> 19:07.897
<i>Did he find the formula to win in one-on-one just like that?</i>

19:07.981 --> 19:09.823
I can control the ball behind me.

19:10.037 --> 19:11.310
I won't lose anymore.

19:11.400 --> 19:13.400
Bastard.

19:13.480 --> 19:14.860
I'll crush you.

19:14.940 --> 19:15.900
Yes.

19:18.650 --> 19:20.910
Come, Isagi. Let's both pressure him.

19:20.990 --> 19:23.280
What? What about Naruhaya?

19:23.370 --> 19:24.580
No problem.

19:25.240 --> 19:29.160
<i>He's the king. After losing to us, he's in no state to pass.</i>

19:29.750 --> 19:31.250
Barou! I'm open!

19:31.330 --> 19:32.750
Shut up, small fry.

19:32.830 --> 19:34.130
I...

19:34.210 --> 19:35.130
Got it!

19:35.210 --> 19:37.130
Nice, Isagi! Send it!

19:37.210 --> 19:38.340
I won't allow it!

19:39.130 --> 19:40.970
<i>Nagi's weapon is ball control.</i>

19:41.050 --> 19:43.390
<i>Against Nagi, who can turn a ball coming from behind like earlier</i>

19:43.470 --> 19:45.600
<i>into a goal,</i>

19:45.680 --> 19:48.600
<i>the defense will position themselves so he can't turn forward.</i>

19:49.350 --> 19:50.600
<i>Taking advantage of that,</i>

19:50.690 --> 19:53.230
<i>he'll get past the opponent with an unpredictable first touch.</i>

19:53.310 --> 19:56.230
<i>That's Nagi's one-on-one strategy!</i>

19:56.320 --> 19:58.610
<i>But they're already on guard against that.</i>

19:58.690 --> 20:02.610
<i>So next time, against defenses that keep their distance like Naruhaya,</i>

20:02.700 --> 20:06.580
<i>Nagi, utilizing the gap that forms,</i>

20:06.660 --> 20:10.540
<i>will be able to advance and create plays as he wishes.</i>

20:11.210 --> 20:16.340
<i>So a pass sent to Nagi can even be as hard as a shot.</i>

20:16.420 --> 20:19.460
<i>This time, different from before,</i>

20:19.550 --> 20:20.590
<i>it will be a soft,</i>

20:22.010 --> 20:23.760
<i>'black hole' control!</i>

20:23.840 --> 20:27.560
<i>Since Naruhaya kept his distance, he can't block the shot.</i>

20:27.640 --> 20:29.640
<i>This is Nagi's power.</i>

20:29.720 --> 20:32.390
<i>A control that gives life to the ball and</i>

20:32.480 --> 20:35.520
<i>a control that kills the ball.</i>

20:35.610 --> 20:38.150
<i>By using these two controls,</i>

20:39.190 --> 20:41.820
<i>Nagi Seishiro's formula is complete!</i>

20:45.410 --> 20:47.780
Alright, 3 more left.

20:47.870 --> 20:51.540
<i>I also want to find a way to win in one-on-one!</i>

20:53.500 --> 20:55.460
Cut the racket, fools.

20:56.710 --> 20:57.840
Both of you,

20:57.920 --> 21:00.420
I can defeat by myself!

21:01.460 --> 21:04.010
<i>Shit! It's the same as Rin!</i>

21:04.680 --> 21:06.470
<i>That was close!</i>

21:06.550 --> 21:08.342
<i>This guy's sense for goal is insane.</i>

21:08.426 --> 21:10.060
<i>I can't let him shoot again.</i>

21:10.140 --> 21:12.180
The loose ball is mine!

21:12.270 --> 21:14.690
<i>Naruhaya? He came so fast!</i>

21:14.770 --> 21:16.060
Pass, small fry!

21:16.150 --> 21:17.650
Got it, king!

21:19.110 --> 21:20.010
Damn it!

21:21.900 --> 21:23.110
<i>Damn it.</i>

21:23.190 --> 21:27.280
<i>The situation is bad. Barou and Nagi's skills are pretty much at the same level.</i>

21:27.370 --> 21:31.240
<i>In that case, this match rests in Naruhaya's and my hands.</i>

21:34.370 --> 21:35.790
Isagi.

21:35.870 --> 21:40.500
Do you know why I wanted to play against you?

21:40.590 --> 21:43.840
Huh? Isn't it because you want Nagi?

21:44.880 --> 21:46.840
Partly true.

21:47.470 --> 21:50.390
My real goal was

21:51.220 --> 21:54.270
because I thought I could defeat you, Isagi.

21:55.890 --> 21:59.860
<i>Since we've fought together until now, I know.</i>

21:59.940 --> 22:03.440
<i>What you can and can't do.</i>

22:03.530 --> 22:07.280
Isagi, you're not someone who can fight head-to-head.

22:08.200 --> 22:09.240
<i>This bastard,</i>

22:09.320 --> 22:15.200
even though you can't score on your own like Chigiri, Kunigami, and Bachira,

22:15.290 --> 22:19.000
you've made it this far by having those around you carry your ass.

22:20.040 --> 22:22.750
You're not a genius like Nagi or Barou.

22:22.840 --> 22:24.590
You and I,

22:25.170 --> 22:27.010
we're both average people.

22:28.090 --> 22:29.340
What are you doing, Isagi?

22:29.430 --> 22:30.680
Pass the ball!

22:32.510 --> 22:33.350
Damn it!

22:33.890 --> 22:34.930
Pathetic.

22:35.020 --> 22:36.560
Isagi, we're stopping it!

22:37.310 --> 22:38.270
<i>Here it comes.</i>

22:38.350 --> 22:40.810
<i>Barou's attack!</i>

22:51.570 --> 22:53.580
-<i>Did he pass?</i>
-Pass it back, small fry.

22:54.870 --> 22:56.040
No way.

22:57.080 --> 22:59.790
<i>I also want to catch up to the geniuses.</i>

23:00.330 --> 23:03.670
<i>Shit! Naruhaya's weapon,</i>

23:03.750 --> 23:05.550
Mine is sneaking behind.

23:06.800 --> 23:11.140
<i>I can't even beat Naruhaya!</i>

23:15.010 --> 23:17.980
<i>Blue Lock, Extra Time.</i>

23:18.060 --> 23:19.440
Welcome.

23:19.520 --> 23:21.270
Nice to meet you again, Bachira.

23:21.350 --> 23:22.440
BACHIRA MEGURU

23:22.520 --> 23:24.520
That was a good bath.

23:24.610 --> 23:27.740
Why are you walking around stark naked?

23:27.820 --> 23:30.990
What? I'm returning to the form I was born in because I'm human.

23:31.070 --> 23:32.620
What kind of argument is that?

23:32.700 --> 23:38.040
<i>Just when I thought I'd made a new friend, he turns out to be weird!</i>

23:38.120 --> 23:39.370
Stark.

23:39.460 --> 23:40.370
What?

23:40.460 --> 23:43.630
I admire your free style, but at least cover your front.

23:43.710 --> 23:46.630
Otherwise, I'll punish you for glamorous exhibitionism.

23:46.710 --> 23:48.420
My bad.

23:48.510 --> 23:50.300
But it feels insanely good.

23:50.380 --> 23:51.550
Should we do it together?

23:51.630 --> 23:52.840
I'm stripping!

23:52.930 --> 23:54.680
ITOSHI RIN

23:54.760 --> 23:57.520
What do you two think you're doing?

23:59.680 --> 24:01.730
Isn't there a 'normal' person in this room?

24:01.810 --> 24:04.040
-You're one to talk?
-You're one to talk?